codex
The exact loop state exposed one avoidable proof nuisance: a temporary local existed only after the first iteration. I’m making the implementation proof-friendly without changing the algorithm—initialize a `next_value` local and preserve `next_value == c` at every loop head. This keeps the invariant faithful to ordinary execution and avoids existentially hiding a changing local.
